  "details": "Currently, avatar creators face significant challenges with third party tools ripping 3D assists and re-uploading or distributing them without authorization.\n\nBecause avatar data is processed client-side, individual asset-level safeguards within Unity Packages are easily stripped out or bypassed during extraction. to address this, I would like to request that VRChat consider implementing automated platform-level verification systems, such as:\n\n* Automated Hash and Signature verification: Identifying known ripped assets files or mesh geometry at the server level during the upload process to prevent unauthorized re-uploads.\n\n* Account Action Protocols: Automatically flagging or restricting accounts that attempt to upload packages matching verified unauthorized signatures.\n\nRipping impacts the entire creator ecosystem, and implementing server-side anti-theft tools would provide creators with much needed security.\n\nThank you for your time and for continuing to support the VRChat community.\n\nBest regards\n\nBeeBootheMayu",
